# Expected failures of mortar (spec/harness.md "Markers"), two forms:
#
#   mortar,<arch>: <reason>
#     run-wide: mortar has no back end there yet, so every mortar link of
#     the architecture is expected to fail.
#   mortar[,<arch>...] <test>.test: <reason>
#     one test (its path under tests/link), on the architectures named
#     (all, when none is): the package that makes it pass, "M2: WP-0xx".
#
# A line takes the place of a test's own xfail(mortar) on that
# architecture (a test's skip still applies; a test may not carry both).
# A mortar link that passes is XPASS, so a line goes when its package
# lands: deleting a package's lines is all it takes.

